@startuml
title PayScale HTTPE - Person-to-Person (P2P) Payment Transaction Sequence

autonumber
actor "Sender Client" as Client
boundary "API Gateway" as Gateway
control "Transaction\nOrchestrator" as Orchestrator
entity "Redis Cluster" as Redis
control "Fraud Detection\nService" as Fraud
database "Sender Shard (PostgreSQL)" as ShardA
database "Receiver Shard (PostgreSQL)" as ShardB
queue "Kafka Topic\n(transaction-events)" as Kafka
actor "Notification Svc\n(WebSocket)" as Notify

== Step 1: Ingestion, Authentication & Rate Limiting ==
Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/payments/p2p\n[Idempotency-Key: UUIDv7, JWT Bearer]
Gateway -> Redis: Check Rate Limit (Lua Token Bucket)
Redis --> Gateway: Allow (Tokens Remaining: 48)
Gateway -> Orchestrator: Forward Request (CorrelationId: txn-892)

== Step 2: Idempotency Reservation ==
Orchestrator -> Redis: SET idempotency:key {hash, IN_FLIGHT} NX EX 86400
alt Idempotency Key Exists (Duplicate Request)
    Redis --> Orchestrator: Key Exists (Return Cached Payload)
    Orchestrator --> Gateway: HTTP 200 OK (Cached Result)
    Gateway --> Client: HTTP 200 OK (No Duplicate Charge)
else New Idempotency Key Reserved
    Redis --> Orchestrator: OK (Reserved)
end

== Step 3: Real-Time Fraud Evaluation (15ms SLA) ==
Orchestrator -> Fraud: POST /evaluate (accountId, amount, ip, device)
Fraud -> Redis: Read User Velocity & Risk Rules
Redis --> Fraud: Velocity = 2 txns/min (Low Risk)
Fraud --> Orchestrator: Fraud Verdict: APPROVED (Latency: 6ms)

alt Fraud Check Failed
    Fraud --> Orchestrator: Fraud Verdict: DENIED (Risk Score > 80)
    Orchestrator -> Redis: UPDATE idempotency:key -> FAILED
    Orchestrator --> Gateway: HTTP 403 Forbidden (Fraud Risk Detected)
    Gateway --> Client: HTTP 403 Forbidden
end

== Step 4: Sender Account Debit & Ledger Journal (Shard A) ==
Orchestrator -> ShardA: BEGIN TRANSACTION
Orchestrator -> ShardA: UPDATE accounts SET available_balance = available_balance - 1500,\nversion = version + 1 WHERE account_id = A AND version = v AND available_balance >= 1500
alt Insufficient Balance / OCC Stale Version
    ShardA --> Orchestrator: 0 rows updated
    Orchestrator -> ShardA: ROLLBACK
    Orchestrator -> Redis: UPDATE idempotency:key -> FAILED
    Orchestrator --> Gateway: HTTP 422 Unprocessable (Insufficient Funds / Retry)
    Gateway --> Client: HTTP 422
end

ShardA -> ShardA: INSERT INTO transactions (id, saga_id, amount, status='PROCESSING')
ShardA -> ShardA: INSERT INTO ledger_entries (account_id=A, DEBIT, 1500.0000)
ShardA --> Orchestrator: Sender Debit Success

== Step 5: Receiver Account Credit & Ledger Journal (Shard B) ==
Orchestrator -> ShardB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
Orchestrator -> ShardB: UPDATE accounts SET available_balance = available_balance + 1500,\nledger_balance = ledger_balance + 1500, version = version + 1 WHERE account_id = B
ShardB -> ShardB: INSERT INTO ledger_entries (account_id=B, CREDIT, 1500.0000)

alt Receiver Credit Fails (Compensating Reversal Required)
    ShardB --> Orchestrator: Error: Account Frozen or Network Timeout
    Orchestrator -> ShardA: EXECUTE COMPENSATION SAGA\nUPDATE accounts SET available_balance = available_balance + 1500\nINSERT INTO ledger_entries (account_id=A, REVERSAL, 1500.0000)\nUPDATE transactions SET status = 'REVERSED'
    ShardA --> Orchestrator: Compensation Committed (within 30s)
    Orchestrator -> Kafka: Produce Event: TRANSACTION_REVERSED
    Orchestrator --> Gateway: HTTP 500 / 422 Transaction Reversed
    Gateway --> Client: Transaction Reversed (Funds Restored)
end

ShardB -> ShardB: COMMIT
ShardB --> Orchestrator: Receiver Credit Success

== Step 6: Finalize Sender Ledger & Transaction Outbox ==
Orchestrator -> ShardA: UPDATE accounts SET ledger_balance = ledger_balance - 1500\nUPDATE transactions SET status = 'COMPLETED', completed_at = NOW()\nINSERT INTO outbox_events (event_type='PAYMENT_COMPLETED')
Orchestrator -> ShardA: COMMIT
Orchestrator -> Redis: UPDATE idempotency:key -> COMPLETED (Payload Cache)

== Step 7: Fast Response to Client ==
Orchestrator --> Gateway: HTTP 200 OK (Transaction Receipt)
Gateway --> Client: HTTP 200 OK [Latency: 38ms]

== Step 8: Asynchronous Outbox Streaming & Notifications ==
ShardA -> Kafka: Debezium CDC publishes outbox event to `transaction-events`
Kafka -> Notify: Consume PAYMENT_COMPLETED
Notify -> Client: WebSocket Push: "₹1,500 transferred to Account B"
@enduml
